read.description:
The devices whose state Oscar may tell on the phone. Type to search. Only those you already expose to voice assistants are offered; removing the exposure removes them from Oscar too.

⚠ Sensitive: they tell when your home is empty. Oscar only reads them after your code or your password while the protection is ticked (“Code and protections”).

{sensitive}

control.description:
The devices Oscar may control: turn on or off, open, close, set, run a scene. They are read too. Type to search.

⚠ Those that open your home: Oscar only unlocks, disarms and opens after your code or your password while the protection is ticked. Locking, arming, closing and stopping never require a code.

{opens}
